378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 115 0 R
/T (The list-as-key error. TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'. A dictionary stores each key by its hash value and finds it again by re-computing the hash. A list is mutable - its contents can change after it is used as a key - so its hash would change and the entry would become unreachable. Python therefore refuses to hash lists. A tuple of immutable items never changes, so its hash is stable and it is a valid key. \(A tuple that contains a list is still unhashable, as shown in the output below.\))
/E (The list-as-key error. TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'. A dictionary stores each key by its hash value and finds it again by re-computing the hash. A list is mutable - its contents can change after it is used as a key - so its hash would change and the entry would become unreachable. Python therefore refuses to hash lists. A tuple of immutable items never changes, so its hash is stable and it is a valid key. \(A tuple that contains a list is still unhashable, as shown in the output below.\))
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
