541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 119 0 R
/T (Result. At 100,000 complaints the dictionary loop took 0.29 s and list.count\(\) 2.13 s - 7.4x slower, and the gap widens as either n or d grows \(here d is only 200; a real vocabulary has tens of thousands of words\). get\(\) and setdefault\(\) perform the same. Counter was not faster in this test: most of the time is spent in tokenising \(lower-casing, stripping punctuation and splitting\), which all four methods share, and I fed Counter a generator rather than a ready list of words.)
/E (Result. At 100,000 complaints the dictionary loop took 0.29 s and list.count\(\) 2.13 s - 7.4x slower, and the gap widens as either n or d grows \(here d is only 200; a real vocabulary has tens of thousands of words\). get\(\) and setdefault\(\) perform the same. Counter was not faster in this test: most of the time is spent in tokenising \(lower-casing, stripping punctuation and splitting\), which all four methods share, and I fed Counter a generator rather than a ready list of words.)
