623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 120 0 R
/T (For 100,000 complaints a day I would deploy a dictionary-based count - collections.Counter or the get\(\) loop. It is O\(n\) and linear in the measurements, simple, and its memory is O\(d\). Counter adds most_common\(k\), which gets the top k without sorting the whole dictionary \(O\(d log k\)\), and states the intention clearly, which is why I prefer it for maintenance even though it was not faster here. list.count\(\) is O\(n x d\) and would grow quadratically as the vocabulary grows, so it is rejected.)
/E (For 100,000 complaints a day I would deploy a dictionary-based count - collections.Counter or the get\(\) loop. It is O\(n\) and linear in the measurements, simple, and its memory is O\(d\). Counter adds most_common\(k\), which gets the top k without sorting the whole dictionary \(O\(d log k\)\), and states the intention clearly, which is why I prefer it for maintenance even though it was not faster here. list.count\(\) is O\(n x d\) and would grow quadratically as the vocabulary grows, so it is rejected.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [56]
>>
endobj
