625 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 120 0 R
/T (list.count\(\) for every distinct word \(code above\): O\(n x d\) time - measured 120,000,000 element comparisons at 100,000 complaints - and O\(n + d\) space \(the full word list plus the result\). Counter: O\(n\) time and O\(d\) space, with no word list needed when it is fed a generator; it is a dictionary subclass, so the same hash-table reasoning applies. The dictionary loop and Counter are asymptotically identical; the difference between them is convenience, not complexity.)
/E (list.count\(\) for every distinct word \(code above\): O\(n x d\) time - measured 120,000,000 element comparisons at 100,000 complaints - and O\(n + d\) space \(the full word list plus the result\). Counter: O\(n\) time and O\(d\) space, with no word list needed when it is fed a generator; it is a dictionary subclass, so the same hash-table reasoning applies. The dictionary loop and Counter are asymptotically identical; the difference between them is convenience, not complexity.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [58]
>>
endobj
