659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 121 0 R
/T (Python hashes it and checks the slot; if an equal item is already there nothing is added, so a duplicate registration - the same register number twice - collapses into one. Why membership is faster. x in list compares x with items one by one: O\(n\). x in set hashes x and inspects one slot: O\(1\) on average. Why sets cannot contain lists but can contain tuples. Set members must be hashable, which requires an unchanging value; a list can change, so it is unhashable \(TypeError shown in the output\), while a tuple of hashable items cannot change and is hashable.)
/E (Python hashes it and checks the slot; if an equal item is already there nothing is added, so a duplicate registration - the same register number twice - collapses into one. Why membership is faster. x in list compares x with items one by one: O\(n\). x in set hashes x and inspects one slot: O\(1\) on average. Why sets cannot contain lists but can contain tuples. Set members must be hashable, which requires an unchanging value; a list can change, so it is unhashable \(TypeError shown in the output\), while a tuple of hashable items cannot change and is hashable.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [33]
>>
