1080 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 129 0 R
/T (An index turns "search everything" into "jump to the right place": the work is done once when the index is built, and every later query touches only the relevant entries. The trade-off is extra memory \(here about 8 MB for 115,000 stops\), build time, and maintenance - whenever a train is added, removed or re-timed, the index must be updated or it will return stale answers. It pays off when queries are frequent and updates are rare, which is the case at an enquiry counter.)
/E (An index turns "search everything" into "jump to the right place": the work is done once when the index is built, and every later query touches only the relevant entries. The trade-off is extra memory \(here about 8 MB for 115,000 stops\), build time, and maintenance - whenever a train is added, removed or re-timed, the index must be updated or it will return stale answers. It pays off when queries are frequent and updates are rare, which is the case at an enquiry counter.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
