1090 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 130 0 R
/T (Rules for "same person". \(1\) Two contacts are the same person if they share a normalised phone number - the number is the strongest identifier, and formats "+91 98400 12345", "09840012345" and "9840012345" must count as equal. \(2\) A contact with no valid number is matched on a shared \(case-insensitive\) e-mail address. \(3\) Names are never used for matching - "ravi kumar" and "Dr. Ravi" differ in spelling, and two different people can have the same name. \(4\) Sharing is transitive: if A shares a number with B and B shares another with C, all three are one person. A contact with nothing to match on stays alone.)
/E (Rules for "same person". \(1\) Two contacts are the same person if they share a normalised phone number - the number is the strongest identifier, and formats "+91 98400 12345", "09840012345" and "9840012345" must count as equal. \(2\) A contact with no valid number is matched on a shared \(case-insensitive\) e-mail address. \(3\) Names are never used for matching - "ravi kumar" and "Dr. Ravi" differ in spelling, and two different people can have the same name. \(4\) Sharing is transitive: if A shares a number with B and B shares another with C, all three are one person. A contact with nothing to match on stays alone.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
