/Title (Why a list is suitable. The data are ordered by date, of one kind, and read far more often than they change, so index access \(O\(1\)\) and slicing are exactly what is needed, and one reading per day gives a natural day-number to index mapping. Measured on 365,000 readings: append 0.04 us \(amortised O\(1\)\), pop\(\) 2.21 us \(O\(1\); this figure includes timer overhead\), insert in the middle 81 us and at the front 176 us \(O\(n\): later items shift\), pop\(0\) 134 us \(O\(n\)\), sort\(\) 24.3 ms on random data \(O\(n log n\)\) but 0.9 ms on already sorted data \(Timsort is O\(n\) there\).)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1572 0 R
/Prev 1681 0 R
/Next 1849 0 R
>>
endobj
