/Title (81 us in the middle and 176 us at the front of 365,000 items. For one reading in a 365-item year this is a few microseconds - negligible - so a list is still fine for the village station. A better design, though, avoids inserting at all: pre-fill the list with one slot per day \(None for a missing reading\) so a late reading is simply readings[day] = value, O\(1\). If readings arrive out of order frequently and in large numbers, a dictionary keyed by date is the better structure.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1685 0 R
/Prev 1794 0 R
>>
