/Title (An index turns "search everything" into "jump to the right place": the work is done once when the index is built, and every later query touches only the relevant entries. The trade-off is extra memory \(here about 8 MB for 115,000 stops\), build time, and maintenance - whenever a train is added, removed or re-timed, the index must be updated or it will return stale answers. It pays off when queries are frequent and updates are rare, which is the case at an enquiry counter.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1859 0 R
>>
endobj
1881 0 obj
