/Title (The list-as-key error. TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'. A dictionary stores each key by its hash value and finds it again by re-computing the hash. A list is mutable - its contents can change after it is used as a key - so its hash would change and the entry would become unreachable. Python therefore refuses to hash lists. A tuple of immutable items never changes, so its hash is stable and it is a valid key. \(A tuple that contains a list is still unhashable, as shown in the output below.\))
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1898 0 R
>>
