/Title (Sparse dictionary grid. Store only the zones that have passengers: counts = defaultdict\(int\); counts[\(row, col\)] += 1. Access is O\(1\) average in both designs \(list-of-lists index twice; dictionary hash the tuple once\). Space is O\(rows x cols\) for the list of lists versus O\(number of non-empty zones\) for the dictionary. Measured for a 1000 x 1000 grid with 4 occupied zones: 8,064,856 bytes versus 224 bytes. The price is speed per access: 46.7 ms versus 19.0 ms for 1,000,000 reads, because hashing a tuple costs more than two index operations. Use the list of lists when most zones are used; the dictionary when most are empty.)
