/Title (Why price comes before received. Both occur twice. The sort key is \(-count, word\): the negated count puts the highest count first, and when counts are equal Python compares the second element, the words, alphabetically - "price" < "received" because 'p' comes before 'r'. The second line of the output shows what happens if only the count is used: the tie keeps insertion order \(sorting is stable\) and received comes first, so the explicit tie-breaker is needed.)
