2023 0 obj
<<
/Title (For 100,000 complaints a day I would deploy a dictionary-based count - collections.Counter or the get\(\) loop. It is O\(n\) and linear in the measurements, simple, and its memory is O\(d\). Counter adds most_common\(k\), which gets the top k without sorting the whole dictionary \(O\(d log k\)\), and states the intention clearly, which is why I prefer it for maintenance even though it was not faster here. list.count\(\) is O\(n x d\) and would grow quadratically as the vocabulary grows, so it is rejected.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2002 0 R
>>
endobj
