/Title (Result. A list lookup took 177 us at 10,000 items, 883 us at 100,000 and 12.4 ms at 1,000,000: a hundred times more items cost 70x more time \(the 10,000-item figure varied by about 2x between two runs of this program, so it is the least reliable of the three; the trend is what matters\), consistent with O\(n\). The set lookup stayed at about 0.03-0.05 us whatever the size, consistent with O\(1\). Nested loops grow with n x m: the time rose about fourfold each time n doubled, reaching 0.60 s at 8,000 each, whereas & took 1.1 ms. At 100,000 each, nested loops would need 10 billion comparisons, so they were not run; & took 0.02 s there and 0.36 s at 1,000,000. Building the two sets from the lists is included in the set timing.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2045 0 R
/Prev 2094 0 R
>>
