>>
endobj
2128 0 obj
<<
/Title (Python hashes it and checks the slot; if an equal item is already there nothing is added, so a duplicate registration - the same register number twice - collapses into one. Why membership is faster. x in list compares x with items one by one: O\(n\). x in set hashes x and inspects one slot: O\(1\) on average. Why sets cannot contain lists but can contain tuples. Set members must be hashable, which requires an unchanging value; a list can change, so it is unhashable \(TypeError shown in the output\), while a tuple of hashable items cannot change and is hashable.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2112 0 R
/Prev 2127 0 R
>>
endobj
